XaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1be41942cf3c7e97426638d78f6632e7eb5e9d919b3f0184c591f7a2640d9076","event_uuid":"b4064f23-8710-441a-a14f-bd36d0badd1d","position":{"commit_sha":"311df04cdd029fcb24ceda45cc250196c3731498","position":"1785771919572735001-b4064f23-8710-441a-a14f-bd36d0badd1d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"104721e2394d8617be7261bd3a05032c8c831a561412295dbe5f7952e4d0904f","event_uuid":"5a1f0c8a-4c30-4b1e-a922-91c7c4497137","position":{"commit_sha":"c501d94d1485c628edc2c51db0d05abd4ebb9898","position":"1785771921042934001-5a1f0c8a-4c30-4b1e-a922-91c7c4497137"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"f7fdbba7-c33b-4126-96ff-d43c5e0de867","close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC VERIFICATION AGAINST THE MERGED TREE — all four verified. Merged 0c5b43cfa (Gerrit 1286, LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1). This comment also DISCHARGES AC3 \"and recorded\" ON THE TICKET, which is where the audit trail belongs — the decision previously lived only in the commit message, the docstring and a test.\n\nTHE ATTESTED ARCHITECTURAL GUARD HELD — checked FIRST, because this ticket was ORIGINALLY FILED proposing provider.startswith(\"gateway/\"), which would have violated it:\n  grep -c \"startswith\" src/rebar/llm/capabilities.py  =>  0   (zero, in code AND comments)\n  Guard test test_capabilities_module_still_has_no_provider_name_prefix_matching (tests/unit/test_bedrock_provider.py:119) is an AST walk asserting no startswith/endswith Call node anywhere in capabilities.py. UNCHANGED by this commit and GREEN.\n  The shipped fix is SET MEMBERSHIP, not prefix shape:\n    capabilities.py:384  _GATEWAY_PROVIDER_NAMES = frozenset({...})  (5 exact ids)\n    capabilities.py:434  via_gateway = provider in _GATEWAY_PROVIDER_NAMES\n    capabilities.py:439  \"tier\": \"best_effort\" if (base_url or via_gateway) else \"first_class\"\n  The prefix approach originally filed was NOT implemented. Registry membership, zero exceptions, holds.\n  (startswith does appear in a TEST helper, test_verdict_provenance.py:220, to derive the expected set from config.KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES. The ban is scoped to capabilities.py and the test docstring says so.)\n\nAC1 gateway/* stamps best_effort, RED before the fix — CONFIRMED BY EXECUTION, not inference: test_verdict_provenance.py:264 test_gateway_provider_without_base_url_is_best_effort, parametrized over all 5 gateway ids. Running the POST-fix test file against 0c5b43cfa~1 source (PYTHONPATH pinned to the pre-fix tree): 7 failed, 24 passed — the 5 tier params fail on AssertionError plus 2 ImportError on _GATEWAY_PROVIDER_NAMES. The \"fails before the fix\" clause is demonstrated, not assumed.\n\nAC2 no collateral damage: :287 test_direct_providers_with_no_base_url_stay_first_class (anthropic, bedrock, openai, google-cloud, groq, vertexai) and :278 test_gateway_tier_is_not_decided_by_the_provider_names_shape — mygateway, openai-gateway, gateway, gateway-anthropic all stay first_class, which is the anti-prefix-matching rule asserted as BEHAVIOUR. Both pass post-fix AND passed PRE-fix in the RED run, so they are genuinely unchanged rather than newly satisfied.\n\nAC3 endpoint_host — DECIDED: NOT back-filled. A gateway provider keeps endpoint_host = None unless a base_url was actually configured. Rationale: endpoint_host reports what was CONFIGURED, so synthesising a hostname from a provider id would report a value nobody set. Enforced executably at :297 test_gateway_endpoint_host_stays_none_unless_a_base_url_was_actually_configured — None for gateways, \"gw.example.test\" when a base_url IS set. Also in the commit message and the provenance_for docstring (capabilities.py:420-429). Recorded here to close the audit gap.\n\nAC4 lint/typecheck/default selection: Verified +1 on the merged change ran exactly those; stated as inference. Independently the directly relevant modules run green: 124 passed across test_agentic_message_cache, test_verdict_provenance, test_bedrock_provider, test_llm_capabilities, test_pydantic_ai_runner and the execution-mode dispatch interface test.","timestamp":1785770617335581001}],"created_at":1785731268780199001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9dd76a85-b3ff-4fed-827f-2a052417c649","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"96e6-97d1-7295-4939"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nA run behind an opaque gateway signs its verdict as `tier: \"first_class\"`.\n\n`capabilities.py:307-311` derives the tier SOLELY from `cfg.base_url`:\n\n    \"tier\": \"best_effort\" if base_url else \"first_class\"\n\nBut `KNOWN_PROVIDER_NAMES` (`config.py:214-241`) admits `gateway/anthropic`, `gateway/bedrock`,\n`gateway/google-cloud`, `gateway/groq` and `gateway/openai`, and these are LIVE — they appear in\n`_pydantic_ai_known_providers()` and `ProviderSession.provider_factory` delegates them to\n`pydantic_ai.providers.infer_provider`.\n\nA `gateway/anthropic:claude-opus-4-8` run carries NO `base_url`, so it is stamped `first_class` with\n`endpoint_host: None` — even though every byte traversed Pydantic's AI Gateway, an intermediary that\ncan rewrite the request. The docstring one line above describes exactly this defect (\"a run behind an\nopaque gateway still claimed it came from `anthropic:claude-opus-4-8`\") for the base_url case; the\n`gateway/*` provider family slipped through the same hole.\n\nWHY IT MATTERS HERE MORE THAN ELSEWHERE: rebar SIGNS verdicts and stamps the tier. The whole point of\nthe two-tier design is that an attestation consumer can tell how much to trust the provenance. A\ngateway run stamped `first_class` misrepresents provenance in a signed artifact.\n\nThird-party evidence that gateways do rewrite silently: the Vercel AI Gateway has been documented\nsilently downgrading Anthropic's 1-hour prompt cache\n(danielternyak.com/articles/vercel-ai-gateway-downgrades-anthropic-prompt-cache).\n\n## Approach\n\n    tier = \"best_effort\" if (base_url or provider.startswith(\"gateway/\")) else \"first_class\"\n\nOne line. Consider whether `endpoint_host` should also record the gateway rather than `None`, so the\nprovenance names the intermediary instead of omitting it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] A `gateway/*` provider stamps `tier: \"best_effort\"`, proven by a test that fails before the fix.\n- [x] A direct provider with no `base_url` still stamps `first_class` — the existing behaviour is not\n      collateral damage.\n- [x] It is decided and recorded whether `endpoint_host` should name the gateway rather than be `None`.\n- [x] make lint and make typecheck pass by exit code; the default selection is green.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","061c-ecd1-8967-4a76"],["relates_to","96e6-97d1-7295-4939"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"061c-ecd1-8967-4a76","parent_status_uuid":"b4064f23-8710-441a-a14f-bd36d0badd1d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7fe2-eef7-a1ef-4919","ticket_type":"bug","title":"A gateway/* provider signs as tier first_class, misrepresenting provenance in a signed verdict","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a3e12658-0ce3-4fcc-a3f8-7f805a8d74d0","ab4099b8-9e96-49c8-99a0-ca20e3831f16","09bf37f8-291a-40a4-b5ba-bf7f8444b0e1","b9743900-2e6d-476c-83db-ef8efa5a7a96","4d93e16e-6959-4437-9d9a-d2a8085ed3e3","34d610d8-f22b-449d-bc11-2774609dce7f","64297cd2-362f-44da-aa33-ee93db7eb0db","1adc5f24-2b99-4ab1-89c2-3e17d8f053a5","12a69acc-0d69-4a22-9c61-8649d56d1d7e","a929a064-f470-4bf1-9ff3-276fdb688112","b4064f23-8710-441a-a14f-bd36d0badd1d","5a1f0c8a-4c30-4b1e-a922-91c7c4497137"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659627389421001,"uuid":"6299c275-e918-462c-abac-850cb551fa6c"}